-- pairs-v5.sql  (task #359)  -  the morning check of the 1-hour MACD e-mails for the FIVE PAIRS (USD/JPY, EUR/JPY, AUD/JPY, EUR/USD, AUD/USD), rule v5.
-- ONE read-only statement (WITH ... SELECT) for mcp__Supabase__execute_sql. Replace the two markers START_MS and END_MS (each written once, in double curly braces, in the first CTE) by the epoch
-- milliseconds of the range: bars are judged by their OPEN time, START_MS <= open < END_MS; the Routine's day is (X-2d) 21:00 UTC .. (X-1d) 21:00 UTC,
-- END_MS = START_MS + 86400000. Nothing else is to be edited. Bars that opened before 2026-10-15 21:00 UTC (1792098000000) were judged by an earlier rule: use pairs-v4.min.sql
-- (from 2026-10-14 21:00 UTC) or pairs.min.sql (before that) for those days.
-- It recounts the rule macdx_12_26_9_w600_1h_x80of120_v5 (signal-alerts v29: the MACD line, the blue line, crosses its signal line at 80% or more of the way from the zero
-- line to the top (a SELL, downward) or bottom (a BUY, upward) of the MACD pane of the newest 120 bars) from public.gmo_kline_files as production reads the data, and compares
-- the expected fires with public.signal_alerts (kind signal, interval 1h, that rule id).
-- It reads no user_id / event_id / e-mail address and writes nothing.
-- Result: columns row_type (RUN | SUMMARY | LINE), instrument, bar_open_utc, side, verdict, data (json). See README.md for every field.
-- Written to be run in well under a minute (one day: about 1 second).
